    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n80647" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πένταθλ-ος</span></b> , Lyr. and 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεντάεθλος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who
				practises the</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πένταθλον</span> or <i>conquers
			therein</i>, <i><span class="en">
				B.
				8.27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1361b10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.737f
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἀνήρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					9.75
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				42(1).99.19
			</span></i> (Epid.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			metaph., of <i>one who tries everything</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Amat.</u>
				138e
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν φιλοσοφίᾳ π</span>.
				<i>versed in every department</i> of philosophy, <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				9.37
			</span></i> ; in depreciation, 'jack of all trades', <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				4.7.5
			</span></i>.</div>
